// SWARM RABBIT HOLE — Wave 10 / DIFF-4 (Impl-O): the ALIAS closure —
// the second seam of A6c. `pool<int> q = gfr` (or passing `gfr` by
// value into a `pool<T>`-typed parameter) would rebind a global pool
// under a LOCAL name: locals accept unguarded mutation (their
// "single-thread by construction" story is a LIE once the local
// aliases a global), and the declared mode cannot follow the alias —
// the mode table is keyed by the declared name. Pool objects are
// therefore not copyable values: only handles (ints) cross, and the
// pool is used by its declared name. All three alias forms are
// rejected: the declaration alias, the assignment alias, and the
// parameter alias.
//
// This file is a compile-FAIL golden case (tests/golden.rs).

pool<int> gall = pool_new<int>(8)

fn take(pool<int> p) {
    int h = p.insert(1)
}

fn main() {
    pool<int> q = gall            // E0803: declaration alias
    q = gall                      // E0803: assignment alias
    take(gall)                    // E0803: parameter alias
}
